d Supported File Types (Embedded Edition and Premium Edition).\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Intelligent Technologies\nLatest Revision: 2024-12-23\nValid as Of: 2024-12-23\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1700 ---\nComponent: SAP Document AI\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Supported Languages for Extraction Using Template\nDescription: SAP Document AI now supports additional languages for extraction using template.  See Supported Languages.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Intelligent Technologies\nLatest Revision: 2024-12-23\nValid as Of: 2024-12-23\nVersion: Cloud\n\n", "--- Record 691 ---\nComponent: Cloud Transport Management\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: SAP Cloud Transport Management service available on new data centers.\nDescription: SAP Cloud Transport Management service is now also available in the following regions:  Amazon Web Services in the US West (Oregon) region  Azure in the Canada Central (Toronto) region  See:   SAP Cloud Transport Management in SAP Discovery Center  Regions and API Endpoints Available for the Cloud Foundry Environment  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Application Development and Integration\nLatest Revision: 2025-06-06\nValid as Of: 2025-06-06\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 692 ---\nComponent: Cloud Transport Management\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Smaller UI changes\nDescription: Title Bar    Some functions that were previously found under the logon e-mail address are now available under the new    Application Settings button.      The logon e-mail address was replaced by a User Profile icon.      See:   SAP Cloud Transport Management Home Screen    Import Queue    New Node Details tab displaying general information about a node as well as information about import scheduling.      The Disable Import and Enable Automatic Import buttons were moved to the top right of the UI.      See:   Using the Import Queue  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Application Development and Integration\nLatest Revision: 2025-06-06\nValid as Of: 2025-06-06\nVersion: 2505a\n\n--- Record 693 ---\nComponent: SAP Translation Hub\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle:   Support for LLM-based translation in Document Translation  \nDescription:   Document Translation user interface: Document Translation now supports LLM-based translation as an additional translation provider. Leveraging Large Language Models (LLMs) via SAP's generative AI hub, you can now translate text and files using LLMs in Document Translation to and from 54+ languages, enabling over 2800 language combinations. LLM-based translation is recommended when you translate non-SAP content or content with source-quality challenges like typos and grammar errors.   \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-06-06\nValid as Of: 2025-06-06\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 694 ---\nComponent: Data Attribute Recommendation\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: AI API SDK Tutorial\nDescription: The tutorial Consume the SDK for Data Attribute Recommendation using the AI API from SAP AI Core is now available.  See AI API Tutorials.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-06-05\nValid as Of: 2025-06-05\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 695 ---\nComponent: Mobile Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: End of Life: Mobile Transaction Bridge\nDescription: Mobile Transaction Bridge on SAP Mobile Services will not be available after December 31, 2025. For more information, see SAP Note 3575568.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-06-05\nValid as Of: 2025-06-05\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 696 ---\nComponent: Mobile Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Manage Device Access\nDescription: Admins can create and bind security tokens specifically for applications. This enhances authentication by providing a second-factor verification step on devices managed by Intune. For more information, see Configuring Device Verification Settings.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-06-05\nValid as Of: 2025-06-05\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 697 ---\nComponent: Mobile Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: UI Change: Privacy Statement\nDescription: Now, you can access the Privacy Statement from the User Profile menu too. Learn more about the Data Privacy Statement.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-06-05\nValid as Of: 2025-06-05\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 698 ---\nComponent: Mobile Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Upgrade Service Plan for Single (SaaS) app cockpit\nDescription: Allow admin to upgrade & downgrade their service plan.    Upgrade to build-default: Upgrade existing kernel-service plan to build-default or resources. Upgrading the service plan unlocks advanced features for the application.  Downgrade to kernel-service: Downgrading the service plan clears all advanced features data, including Application Management Policies and Cloud Build.     For more information, see Changing Service Plans for Single (SaaS) Applications.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-06-05\nValid as Of: 2025-06-05\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 699 ---\nComponent: SAP Omnichannel Promotion Pricing\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: New Apps Maintain Coupons and Configure Coupon Code Generation for Coupon Management\nDescription: You can use the Maintain Coupons app to create and maintain coupons. With the Configure Coupon Code Generation app, you can configure parameters such as the code length or code pattern that are then considered during the coupon code generation.  For more information about the apps, see Coupon Management and Configure Coupon Code Generation as well as the in-app help.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business", ": New Apps Maintain Coupons and Configure Coupon Code Generation for Coupon Management\nDescription: You can use the Maintain Coupons app to create and maintain coupons. With the Configure Coupon Code Generation app, you can configure parameters such as the code length or code pattern that are then considered during the coupon code generation.  For more information about the apps, see Coupon Management and Configure Coupon Code Generation as well as the in-app help.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-06-05\nValid as Of: 2025-06-05\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 700 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: Applications\nDescription: We have extended the application search in the administration console. Now you can filter the list items in the search field by typing the name, display name, application ID, organization ID, and client ID.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-06-04\nValid as Of: 2025-06-04\nVersion: 27915\n\n", "--- Record 3341 ---\nComponent: Data Attribute Recommendation\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Resuse of Dataset Schemas\nDescription: We’ve fixed an issue related to the resuse of dataset schemas.  You can now reuse the same dataset schema with different datasets.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-03-06\nValid as Of: 2024-03-06\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3342 ---\nComponent: Mobile Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Download client logs related to crash reports\nDescription: (Version 2402) When a crash occurs, you can now download any available client log files that are related to the crash report, to help analyze the crash. Previously, the related client logs were not made available to download, so you needed to search for the data manually.  See     Viewing Crash Group Analytics      Configuring Mobile Client Log Upload    \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-02-27\nValid as Of: 2024-03-06\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3343 ---\nComponent: Edge Integration Cell\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: API Artifact\nDescription: You can now create an OData API artifact using a .edmx file. This functionality enables users to easily generate and manage OData APIs by leveraging existing .edmx files.   See: Create an API Artifact Using URL\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-03-05\nValid as Of: 2024-03-05\nVersion: 2313\n\n--- Record 3344 ---\nComponent: Edge Integration Cell\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Software Version Update\nDescription:     Edge Integration Cell: 8.13.*      Increment: 2313    \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-03-05\nValid as Of: 2024-03-05\nVersion: 2313\n\n--- Record 3345 ---\nComponent: Graph\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Manage Business Data Graphs using Graph Configuration API\nDescription: The Graph Configuration API simplifies the process of managing your business data graphs automatically. Whether you need to create, update, or delete business data graphs, this API provides an automated option to achieve these tasks.  The primary focus is to enable a seamless integration of business data graph management with your existing CI/CD pipelines.  For more information, see:     Configure Entitlement for Graph      Manage Business Data Graphs using Graph Configuration API    \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Intelligent Technologies\nLatest Revision: 2024-03-05\nValid as Of: 2024-03-05\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3346 ---\nComponent: Kyma Runtime\nEnvironment: Kyma\nTitle: API Gateway module: Update to version 2.2.0\nDescription: Version 2.2.0 of the API Gateway module brings the following changes:    We've introduced PodDisruptionBudget for Ory Oathkeeper. For more information, see the PR.      We've extended APIRule access strategies with no_auth to restrict accessible methods, thereby minimizing the exposure of the API.      Now, the Kyma modules use consistent labeling. To learn more about the labels that the API Gateway module uses, see Labeling Resources.      The API Gateway custom resources (CR) use the Warning state instead of Error when there is more than one APIGateway CR on the cluster. For more information, see the PR.    \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-02-20\nValid as Of: 2024-03-05\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3347 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Apps\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Mobile\nDescription:   Enabled SAP Mobile Services  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-03-05\nValid as Of: 2024-03-05\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3348 ---\nComponent: SAP S/⁠4HANA Cloud for Credit Integration\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Integration with new credit agency: Informa D&B Spain\nDescription: The credit agency Informa D&B Spain is now connected to SAP S/⁠4HANA Cloud for credit integration.  More information:  Available Credit Agency Products and Features  Your Tasks for Integrating a New Credit Agency\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Finance\nLatest Revision: 2024-03-05\nValid as Of: 2024-03-05\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3349 ---\nComponent: Kyma Runtime\nEnvironment: Kyma\nTitle: Istio and API Gateway modules: temporary downtime in the fast channel\nDescription: We plan to eliminate technical debt in the Istio and API Gateway modules on the default Kyma domain in the fast channel. This will take place outside of the maintenance window and might result in a temporary downtime lasting several minutes.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-03-04\nValid as Of: 2024-03-04\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3350 ---\nComponent: Kyma", " technical debt in the Istio and API Gateway modules on the default Kyma domain in the fast channel. This will take place outside of the maintenance window and might result in a temporary downtime lasting several minutes.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-03-04\nValid as Of: 2024-03-04\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3350 ---\nComponent: Kyma Runtime\nEnvironment: Kyma\nTitle: Smaller Machine Types available\nDescription: Smaller Machine Types offering 2 virtual CPUs and 8GB of RAM are available to help you optimize the size of a default Kyma runtime installation and thus reduce its cost.  They include:     m6i.large and m5.large on Amazon Web Services      n2-standard-2 on Google Cloud      Standard_D2s_v5 on Microsoft Azure      These Machine Types are established as the default options and can be specifically selected during both the provisioning process and any future updates. For more information, visit Provisioning and Updating Parameters in the Kyma Environment.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-03-04\nValid as Of: 2024-03-04\nVersion: Cloud\n\n", "--- Record 2431 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: ABAP Development Tools for Eclipse: Specifying \"Empty Key\" Key Definition for Table Types\nDescription: You can now specify Empty Key as a Primary Key Definition for a table type.  See Working with Table Types.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-08-16\nValid as Of: 2024-08-16\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2408\n\n--- Record 2432 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: ABAP Development Tools for Eclipse: Working with the Core Schema Notation Model Object Type\nDescription: The Core Schema Notation Model workbench object is a container for the imported Core Schema Notation (CSN) documents and the derived CSN model. The CSN documents can be manually uploaded into the Core Schema Notation Model workbench object.  See Working with the Core Schema Notation Model.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-08-16\nValid as Of: 2024-08-16\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2408\n\n--- Record 2433 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Add Custom Logo to Fiori Launchpad\nDescription: You can now exchange the SAP logo in the SAP Fiori launchpad with a customer logo. For administrators, there is a new parameter COMPANY_LOGO_URL in the Manage Launchpad Settings app. Here, you can upload a logo from a file. This logo will replace the SAP logo for all users.  For more information, see Manage Launchpad Settings.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-08-16\nValid as Of: 2024-08-16\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2408\n\n--- Record 2434 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Annotation: ObjectModel.supportedCapabilities\nDescription: You can use this annotation to check whether or not the UI use case is supported. If supported, then either the creation of UI projections or alternatively the direct consumption in an UI service binding is possible. Otherwise, warnings or errors occur indicating that the UI usage is not supported and might lead to unexpected errors.  For more information, see the annotation documentation of the ObjectModel domain in KTD.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-08-16\nValid as Of: 2024-08-16\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2408\n\n--- Record 2435 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Annotation: Semantics.valueRange\nDescription: You can use this annotation to inform consumers about the value range of a CDS element, allowing to specify minimal and/or maximal values and indicate whether these are exclusive or inclusive. The annotation can be applied to all fully ordered data types, i.e. Characters, Strings, Numbers, or Data Types.  For more information, see the annotation documentation of the Semantics domain in KTD.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-08-16\nValid as Of: 2024-08-16\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2408\n\n--- Record 2436 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Annotation: UI.dataPoint.title\nDescription: You can use this annotation to define the title of a data point.  For more information, see the annotation documentation of the UI domain in KTD.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-08-16\nValid as Of: 2024-08-16\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2408\n\n--- Record 2437 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Business Configuration App without Transport Option\nDescription:     You can now select the transport option No Transport.      There is a new option to enable a transport request selection bar in the header toolbar.    See Generating a Business Configuration Maintenance Object with the Generate ABAP Repository Objects Wizard\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-08-16\nValid as Of: 2024-08-16\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2408\n\n--- Record 2438 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: CDS Reusable Measures & Filters\nDescription: Managing and aligning analytical reporting might be quite challenging for complex businesses. With the introduction of reusable measures and filters, you can define key figures, measures, formulas, filters and many more features centrally, based on your needs. Those reusable measures and filters can then be utilized by CDS view entities by referencing those reusable artifacts. This ensures a homogenous definition of complex calculations and consolidates existing coherences of your running business.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-08-16\nValid as Of: 2024-08-16\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2408\n\n--- Record 2439 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Communication Arrangements\nDescription: Communication arrangements now also support Communication Targets and Logical External Schema.  For more information, see   .\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType", "\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-08-16\nValid as Of: 2024-08-16\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2408\n\n--- Record 2439 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Communication Arrangements\nDescription: Communication arrangements now also support Communication Targets and Logical External Schema.  For more information, see   .\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-07-09\nValid as Of: 2024-08-16\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2408\n\n--- Record 2440 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Creation of Local ABAP CDS Models Based on imported CDS Models\nDescription: Do you have an existing CDS Model that was created via CAP Core Data Services, the LCAP Modeler in BAS or One Domain Model and you want to transfer it into you ABAP Cloud stack? You can import these external CDS models via the CSN-import and create a local CSN object model, You can generate an ABAP CDS data model based on the imported CSN model.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-08-16\nValid as Of: 2024-08-16\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2408\n\n", "--- Record 1521 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: Provisioning sub-attributes of emails attribute\nDescription: Changes in the read transformations of Identity Authentication (version 1 and 2), Local Identity Directory, and SAP Ariba Invoice Management ensure that Identity Provisioning now reads all sub-attributes of the emails attribute as defined in the SCIM core schema (that is, value, type, primary, display).  Changes in the write and proxy write transformations of Identity Authentication (version 2) ensure that users with multiple email addresses are provisioned with the correct primary email.  For more information, see Identity Authentication (Source), Identity Authentication (Target), Identity Authentication (Proxy).\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-01-29\nValid as Of: 2025-01-29\nVersion: 27344\n\n--- Record 1522 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: Reduced Set of Scopes for Credentials of Cloud Identity Services Instances\nDescription: When you create a new binding or service key for a service instance of Cloud Identity Services with the application plan, the generated credential only has the following scopes depending on the credential type:      Certificates: OpenID and Identity Directory for Applications.      Secrets and JSON Web Key Sets: OpenID.      If the application needs additional scopes, such as Application or Application Users, the tenant administrator must explicitly grant them.  For more information about configuring client credentials, see Configure Secrets for API Authentication.  For more information about using SAP Cloud Identity Services with SAP BTP, see Integrating the Service with the Identity Service of SAP BTP.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-01-29\nValid as Of: 2025-01-29\nVersion: 27344\n\n--- Record 1523 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: Regular Upgrade\nDescription: Cloud Identity Services have been upgraded.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-01-29\nValid as Of: 2025-01-29\nVersion: 27344\n\n--- Record 1524 ---\nComponent: Continuous Integration & Delivery\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Sporadic Internal Server Errors Resolved\nDescription: A temporary issue that caused failed operations in the service user interface has been resolved.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-01-29\nValid as Of: 2025-01-29\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1525 ---\nComponent: Decentralized Identity Verification\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Sign Revocation Lists\nDescription: A revocation list can now be signed, and its signature is validated during verification.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-01-01\nValid as Of: 2025-01-29\nVersion: 3.6\n\n--- Record 1526 ---\nComponent: Identity Provisioning\nEnvironment: Neo\nTitle: Group mapping changes\nDescription: The default read and proxy read transformations of SAP Ariba Applications and SAP Analytics Cloud (SCIM API version 1 and 2) provisioning systems are extended to support the provisioning of application-specific groups.  These transformations include type and supportedOperations group attributes.  The read transformations of these provisioning systems are also extended with a condition that checks whether the ips.application.id property contains a value and is not null.  For more information, refer to the relevant connector documentation under Supported Systems.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-01-29\nValid as Of: 2025-01-29\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1527 ---\nComponent: Identity Provisioning\nEnvironment: Neo\nTitle: Invalid mapping in SAP AS ABAP\nDescription: An invalid mapping containing the valueMapping type has been removed from the SAP AS ABAP read and proxy read transformations. Systems created before January 14, 2025, will need to fix this issue by following the instructions in SAP Note 3562746 .\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-01-29\nValid as Of: 2025-01-29\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1528 ---\nComponent: Identity Provisioning\nEnvironment: Neo\nTitle: New conditional functions implemented\nDescription: The conditional function isApplicationSpecificGroup is implemented to verify whether a group is associated with a particular application configured in SAP Cloud Identity Services - Identity Authentication.  The conditional functions IsAttributeWithOptionalPrefix and IsAttributeWithMandatoryPrefix can be used to verify wheter an attribute value starts with an optional or predefined mandatory prefix.  Currently, they are implemented for SAP Advanced Financial Closing, SAP Ariba Applications, and SAP Analytics Cloud (SCIM API version 1 and 2) provisioning systems.  For more information, refer to the relevant connector documentation under Supported Systems and Transformation Functions. \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-01-29\nValid as Of: 2025-01-29\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1529 ---\nComponent: Identity Provisioning\nEnvironment: Neo\nTitle: Provisioning sub-", "IM API version 1 and 2) provisioning systems.  For more information, refer to the relevant connector documentation under Supported Systems and Transformation Functions. \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-01-29\nValid as Of: 2025-01-29\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1529 ---\nComponent: Identity Provisioning\nEnvironment: Neo\nTitle: Provisioning sub-attributes of emails attribute\nDescription: Changes in the read transformations of Identity Authentication (version 1 and 2) and SAP Ariba Invoice Management ensure that Identity Provisioning now reads all sub-attributes of the emails attribute as defined in the SCIM core schema (that is, value, type, primary, display).  Changes in the write and proxy write transformations of Identity Authentication (version 2) ensure that users with multiple email addresses are provisioned with the correct primary email.  For more information, see Identity Authentication (Source), Identity Authentication (Target), Identity Authentication (Proxy).  The default read transformations of Identity Authentication and SAP Ariba Central Invoice Management provisioning systems are changed to support reading of all available email attributes in the target system.  For more information, see Identity Authentication and SAP Ariba Central Invoice Management.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-01-29\nValid as Of: 2025-01-29\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1530 ---\nComponent: Joule\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Roles based access for the Joule Standalone Web Client\nDescription: Roles based access has been introduced for the Joule Standalone Web Client.  You will be able to login to the Standalone Joule Web Client only if you have the end_user or capability_developer role assigned in SAP BTP.  The login will fail, if the required role is missing. \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-01-29\nValid as Of: 2025-01-29\nVersion: Cloud\n\n"], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small"}}, "key": "embeddings_be6ee4fcb252dd0bdea3213eae0a7614ccbfcbc1347d616d839c4e4986f51735_v2"}